    "terminalReason": "completed",
    "text": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack in Cuis with comprehensive tests. Here's what was created:\n\n## BoundedStack Class (category: 'BoundedStack')\n\n**Instance Methods:**\n- `push:` \u2014 adds an object to the stack; fails with \"stack is full\" if at capacity\n- `pop` \u2014 removes and returns the top object; fails with \"stack is empty\" if empty\n- `top` \u2014 returns the top object without removing it; fails with \"stack is empty\" if empty\n- `isEmpty` \u2014 returns whether the stack is empty\n- `size` \u2014 returns the number of objects in the stack\n\n**Class-Side Creation:**\n- `capacity:` \u2014 creates a stack with the given capacity; fails with \"capacity must be a positive integer\" if not a positive integer\n\n## Test Suite (category: 'BoundedStack-Tests')\n\n**13 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Valid stack creation with positive capacity\n- Invalid capacities (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Pushing objects and size tracking\n- Popping with LIFO ordering\n- Top access without removal\n- Full stack rejection\n- Empty stack error cases\n- State consistency after errors\n\nAll 13 tests pass. The implementation follows the design heuristics with proper error messages defined as class methods, precondition validation at instance creation, and a single initialize funnel. The packages are unsaved and ready to file out when you want them."
